implementationPlan.description:
Verification. Run this ONE fresh command from the repo root in WSL; its output is the complete_task evidence. It takes about 5-6 minutes, so raise the Bash tool timeout to 600000 ms or run it in the background.

mkdir -p /mnt/d/moe-scratch && S=$(mktemp -d /mnt/d/moe-scratch/v-31187ec1.XXXXXX) && git archive HEAD scripts | tar -x -C "$S" && for f in scripts/moe-agent.sh scripts/moe-agent.ps1 scripts/tests/postflight-worktree.cjs scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js; do cp "$f" "$S/$f" && cmp "$f" "$S/$f" || exit 1; done && echo "snapshot $S" && cd "$S" && bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh && g='MOE_(WORKTREE|LAND|CONTROL|BOARD)_[A-Z0-9_]*' && diff <(grep -oE "$g" scripts/moe-agent.sh | sort -u) <(grep -oE "$g" scripts/moe-agent.ps1 | sort -u) && grep -q MOE_WORKTREE_CONTEXT_FAILED scripts/moe-agent.sh && bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh && T="$S/scripts/tests" && node "$T/postflight-worktree.cjs" sh "$S/scripts/moe-agent.sh" "$T/postflight-fake-proxy.js" "$S" "$(command -v bash)" && node.exe "$(wslpath -w "$T/postflight-worktree.cjs")" ps1 "$(wslpath -w "$S/scripts/moe-agent.ps1")" "$(wslpath -w "$T/postflight-fake-proxy.js")" "$(wslpath -w "$S")" powershell

The architect dry-ran this exact command at HEAD 920f9cca, with the CONTEXT_FAILED grep stubbed and MOE_WORKTREE_ONLY=shared-landed: rc 0 in 11 s, with sh and PS 5.1 each printing '1 ok, 0 failed'.

Expected output:
- the codes diff is empty and parity-check prints PASS;
- the sh suite prints '[worktree] path-long n/a off win32' and 'N ok, 0 failed';
- the ps1 suite (Windows PowerShell 5.1 via node.exe) prints 'N ok, 0 failed';
- the four new cases print 'ok' in both.

N is 16 for sh and 17 for ps1 at today's case list. It is higher if a peer row (WT-05) added cases before this row.

Put both summary lines and the new-case lines in the step note.

acceptanceCriteria:
Both twins, on a moe/control checkout: a resume (alreadyAssigned, no workspace) whose get_context fails with a JSON-RPC error, answers {}, or answers for another task gets this result:
- the output includes `[ERROR] MOE_WORKTREE_CONTEXT_FAILED: ...`;
- exactly one report_blocked, for this task and seat, whose reason starts with the code;
- no CLI launch, exit 1;
- no W and no moe/task/<id> created;
- the control checkout unchanged.

Both twins: the same failed resume read on a control checkout that is NOT on moe/control launches the CLI exactly as shared mode does today:
- 0 report_blocked;
- no MOE_WORKTREE_ line;
- no W;
- exit 0.
